title:    One route deleted. One path dies, the other does not notice.
subtitle: Nothing else changed - not the VM, not the subnet flag, not the firewall
width:    980
---
route deleted: Private Google Access -> 000   PSC endpoint -> 401

# The only change was deleting the VPC's default route to the internet gateway.
#
# Private Google Access needs that route: the documentation requires "routes
# whose next hops are the default internet gateway", because the traffic is
# going to Google's PUBLIC addresses. Remove it and there is no path.
#
# The PSC endpoint never used it. 10.99.0.2 is inside this VPC, so the packet
# never needs a route off the network at all.
#
# This is what "private" actually buys you, and the two mechanisms are not
# interchangeable - which is invisible until the route is gone.
